<title>SOUTH AFRICA: PEARSON-TML DEAL CLOSE, S.AFRICAN PAPER REPORTS.</title>
<headline>PEARSON-TML DEAL CLOSE, S.AFRICAN PAPER REPORTS.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-12-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Business Times newspaper reported on Sunday that a deal between its owners Times Media Ltd (TML) and Britain's Pearson Plc was likely to be signed within hours.</p>
<p>&quot;Pearson's purchase of a half-stake in TML's Business Day and Financial Mail looks set to be concluded this weekend,&quot; it said. &quot;Reliable sources indicate that the announcement will be made tonight.&quot;</p>
<p>The paper said TML and Pearson -- publishers of the Financial Times -- were expected to form a new company which would house the two business publications and a jointly held television operation.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +2721 252238</p>
